{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ASYV71AKvAK6RioBgkmFLx","type":"tool_result","content":"254\t### Membership is a query\n255\t\n256\tA ReplicaSet does not track its Pods by name and does not hold a list. It has a `.spec.selector`, a label selector, using the labels that identify potential Pods to acquire [source: k8s-docs-replicaset-2026-08-24]. The machinery is exactly what Chapter 4 gave you: `matchLabels` is a map of key/value pairs equivalent to `matchExpressions` with the operator `In`, and newer resources such as Job, Deployment, ReplicaSet and DaemonSet support set-based requirements through both [source: k8s-docs-labels-selectors-2026-08-23]. Nothing new to learn, one new place to apply it. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 4 §5 — labels and selectors, the universal join]*\n257\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"466f6b4a-7e79-4624-b651-f0067f3d5080","uuid":"d1dd5f6c-cd4a-49a2-ac4b-5ac3447fa9e1","timestamp":"2026-08-24T15:39:15.539Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-06\\draft-v1.md","content":"### Membership is a query\n\nA ReplicaSet does not track its Pods by name and does not hold a list. It has a `.spec.selector`, a label selector, using the labels that identify potential Pods to acquire [source: k8s-docs-replicaset-2026-08-24]. The machinery is exactly what Chapter 4 gave you: `matchLabels` is a map of key/value pairs equivalent to `matchExpressions` with the operator `In`, and newer resources such as Job, Deployment, ReplicaSet and DaemonSet support set-based requirements through both [source: k8s-docs-labels-selectors-2026-08-23]. Nothing new to learn, one new place to apply it. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 4 §5 — labels and selectors, the universal join]*\n","numLines":4,"startLine":254,"totalLines":1255}}}
