{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GuZA2npxHB1n1gaZson8zd","type":"tool_result","content":"290\t> **Logbook Entry:** The overlapping-selector failure has a recognizable signature, and it never looks like a configuration mistake, which is what makes it expensive.\n291\t>\n292\t> Somebody ships a second workload and copies the first one's manifest as a starting point, including its labels. Both controllers are now querying for the same Pods. Neither one is misconfigured in any way the API can see; each one's template agrees with its own selector, which is all the API validates. But each controller is now counting Pods the other one created, seeing a total that keeps moving for reasons it did not cause, and correcting toward a number the other controller immediately disagrees with.\n293\t>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"466f6b4a-7e79-4624-b651-f0067f3d5080","uuid":"49e04c76-4caf-4f0a-ba2a-7c581750ef2a","timestamp":"2026-08-24T15:39:16.961Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-06\\draft-v1.md","content":"> **Logbook Entry:** The overlapping-selector failure has a recognizable signature, and it never looks like a configuration mistake, which is what makes it expensive.\n>\n> Somebody ships a second workload and copies the first one's manifest as a starting point, including its labels. Both controllers are now querying for the same Pods. Neither one is misconfigured in any way the API can see; each one's template agrees with its own selector, which is all the API validates. But each controller is now counting Pods the other one created, seeing a total that keeps moving for reasons it did not cause, and correcting toward a number the other controller immediately disagrees with.\n>","numLines":4,"startLine":290,"totalLines":1255}}}
