{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PJtkqMztj5gWggXS7cxZ3j","type":"tool_result","content":"799\t> **Name this shape, because you are going to meet it again.** *The object exists but nothing happens without the component.* An Ingress with no ingress controller is the same shape. `kubectl top` with no metrics-server is the same shape. A vertical autoscaler that isn't shipped by default is the same shape. It is not four gotchas. It is one rule with four instances, and the rule is that Kubernetes will happily accept a record of intent that nothing in the cluster is currently able to act on. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 §4 — Ingress without an ingress controller]* *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §2 — `kubectl top` without metrics-server]*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"466f6b4a-7e79-4624-b651-f0067f3d5080","uuid":"6b4ad8b8-5373-42c7-9923-e7aa055dbe45","timestamp":"2026-08-24T15:39:21.194Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-06\\draft-v1.md","content":"> **Name this shape, because you are going to meet it again.** *The object exists but nothing happens without the component.* An Ingress with no ingress controller is the same shape. `kubectl top` with no metrics-server is the same shape. A vertical autoscaler that isn't shipped by default is the same shape. It is not four gotchas. It is one rule with four instances, and the rule is that Kubernetes will happily accept a record of intent that nothing in the cluster is currently able to act on. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 §4 — Ingress without an ingress controller]* *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §2 — `kubectl top` without metrics-server]*","numLines":1,"startLine":799,"totalLines":1255}}}
